accTitle: Parent and child ownership in B2 recovery
accDescr: The parent request and objective remain owned by the active B4 intention. B2 stores a compact parent identity and version snapshot, delegates a bounded subset of read capabilities to the child investigation, and accepts findings only after the parent identity checks. The child does not receive the full objective or capability grant.
    PARENT[Parent request and objective] --> INTENTION[Active B4 intention]
    INTENTION --> CASE[B2 case with parent identity and version]
    CASE --> CHILD[Bounded child investigation]
    CHILD --> RESULT[Typed findings and assumptions]
    RESULT --> CHECK[Parent and result identity checks]
    CHECK --> RETURN[Return to the same B4 intention]
    RETURN --> INTENTION
    GRANT[Parent capability grant] --> SUBSET[Child capability subset]
    SUBSET --> CASE
    NOTE[No parent objective copy or write capability] -. boundary .-> CHILD
